\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:idea}{{1}{4}{The idea, on the running example of \S \ref {sec:overview}. At a guarded choice in world $W$ the branch whose guard holds is intended; taking another is a misselection. Its severity is a property of the residual, and the three fates drawn are the only three: the goal still reachable (\Ben ), the goal lost with no hazard reachable (\Fut ), or a hazard reachable (\Cat ) --- here by crossing a point of no return, an irreversible capability after which the goal cannot be recovered. In $G_{\mathsf {bad}}$ the misselected branch takes the third}{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:idea@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]4}}
\citation{jongmans-ecoop23}
\citation{castro-popl26}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{5}{Architecture. Compaction from prose to a pack is untrusted and may use a language model; nothing beyond the trust boundary does. The severity classifier runs the discipline's existing reachability search pointwise at every branch of every choice, at every abstract world and budget, and emits a per-branch severity, the tolerance degree $\kstar $, a witness naming the point-of-no-return action, and repair suggestions. The certified pack drives the gated runtime that refuses out-of-protocol attempts}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][4][]5}}
